title: 'pallet-whitelist: permissionless authorized dispatch'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `dispatch_whitelisted_call` and `dispatch_whitelisted_call_with_preimage` gain
    `#[pallet::authorize]` callbacks: an unsigned submission is admitted at the transaction
    pool if `DispatchWhitelistedOrigin::try_origin(Authorized)` passes and the call hash is in
    `WhitelistedCall`. For `dispatch_whitelisted_call` the preimage must additionally be
    available at `call_encoded_len`. `frame_system::AuthorizeCall` converts the `None` origin
    into `Authorized` for the dispatch body. Dispatch bodies are unchanged and no new `Config`
    item is added. `WeightInfo` gains `authorize_*` functions for the authorization weights.

    Submissions are tagged `(call_hash, call_encoded_len, call_weight)`. A too-low
    `call_weight_witness` cannot be caught at the pool without decoding the preimage, so it is
    admitted and fails in-block for free; the tag denies it the slot of the correctly witnessed
    submission.

    Adds `frame_system::EnsureAuthorized`. A runtime opts in by including it in
    `DispatchWhitelistedOrigin`, e.g. `EitherOf<EnsureRoot<AccountId>, EnsureAuthorized<AccountId>>`;
    leaving it out keeps the current behavior.

